          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most concrete paver patios, decide between a color-enhancing acrylic film and an invisible penetrating repellent, then buy a quality product of that type. Foundation Armor AR350 is the forgiving wet-look pick where solvents are allowed, SX5000 WB and Ghostshield Siloxa-Tek 8500 are the low-maintenance natural choices, and DryTreat earns its price only on natural stone.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the result is decided before the pail is opened: clean thoroughly, refill the joints, let the pavers dry completely, and apply thin coats in a good weather window. Get those four things right and an ordinary sealer will outperform an expensive one applied in a hurry.
          </p>
